332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 192 0 R
/T (It is a privilege to present this report on the Local Conference of Youth \(LCOY\) Nepal 2026. Over three days in Kathmandu, young people from all seven provinces came together not to repeat what they had read about climate change, but to put on record what they had lived through: schools shut for two weeks by heat in Madhesh, a bridge collapsing in Kathmandu, water sources drying in Bardiya, springs disappearing in Kavre, a family in Pokhara losing its home to flash floods and many more.)
/E (It is a privilege to present this report on the Local Conference of Youth \(LCOY\) Nepal 2026. Over three days in Kathmandu, young people from all seven provinces came together not to repeat what they had read about climate change, but to put on record what they had lived through: schools shut for two weeks by heat in Madhesh, a bridge collapsing in Kathmandu, water sources drying in Bardiya, springs disappearing in Kavre, a family in Pokhara losing its home to flash floods and many more.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 192 0 R
/T (The theme we chose this year, "Together for Climate Transparency", was deliberate. Nepal is not short of climate commitments. What has been missing is the ability of ordinary people, and young people in particular, to see what is promised, what is funded, what is delivered and what is still missing. Transparency is what turns a grievance into evidence, and evidence into accountability. That idea ran through every session, from the glacier data presented by ICIMOD to the delegate who asked why there was no child on the panel answering questions about children.)
/E (The theme we chose this year, "Together for Climate Transparency", was deliberate. Nepal is not short of climate commitments. What has been missing is the ability of ordinary people, and young people in particular, to see what is promised, what is funded, what is delivered and what is still missing. Transparency is what turns a grievance into evidence, and evidence into accountability. That idea ran through every session, from the glacier data presented by ICIMOD to the delegate who asked why there was no child on the panel answering questions about children.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
