360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 193 0 R
/T (Two demands surfaced in almost every session. First, that children and youth participation stop being tokenistic: delegates repeatedly distinguish between being counted and being consulted, and asked to be present in planning and problem-solving rather than invited as observers and advisors. Second, that transparency be treated as infrastructure rather than a slogan, with accessible data on climate finance flows, project results and local budget allocation. As one panelist put it during the transparency session, youth are not an audience, they are an accountability force.)
/E (Two demands surfaced in almost every session. First, that children and youth participation stop being tokenistic: delegates repeatedly distinguish between being counted and being consulted, and asked to be present in planning and problem-solving rather than invited as observers and advisors. Second, that transparency be treated as infrastructure rather than a slogan, with accessible data on climate finance flows, project results and local budget allocation. As one panelist put it during the transparency session, youth are not an audience, they are an accountability force.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
