/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 194 0 R
/T (The Local Conference of Youth is a national event endorsed by YOUNGO, the official children and youth constituency of the UNFCCC. LCOYs feed into the global Conference of Youth \(COY\) and, through it, into the Conference of the Parties. They exist because only a small number of young people can attend global negotiations in person, and a national platform is needed to build positions that those few delegates can carry.)
/E (The Local Conference of Youth is a national event endorsed by YOUNGO, the official children and youth constituency of the UNFCCC. LCOYs feed into the global Conference of Youth \(COY\) and, through it, into the Conference of the Parties. They exist because only a small number of young people can attend global negotiations in person, and a national platform is needed to build positions that those few delegates can carry.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
379 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 194 0 R
/T (Nepal has hosted an LCOY every year since 2022. LCOY Nepal 2022 was held virtually and engaged more than 60 young people directly and over 2,000 indirectly. LCOY Nepal 2023, themed "Vision to Action", brought together participants from all seven provinces with more than half of them women. LCOY Nepal 2024, organised by YASEN and Sustainability Week Kathmandu under the theme "From Local to Global", convened 190 participants and focused on NDCs, loss and damage and indigenous knowledge. LCOY Nepal 2025, led by Powershift Nepal with partners, engaged around 500 children and young people through virtual, provincial and national events and produced a statement that fed into Nepal's COP 30 priorities and YOUNGO's Global Youth Statement.)
/E (Nepal has hosted an LCOY every year since 2022. LCOY Nepal 2022 was held virtually and engaged more than 60 young people directly and over 2,000 indirectly. LCOY Nepal 2023, themed "Vision to Action", brought together participants from all seven provinces with more than half of them women. LCOY Nepal 2024, organised by YASEN and Sustainability Week Kathmandu under the theme "From Local to Global", convened 190 participants and focused on NDCs, loss and damage and indigenous knowledge. LCOY Nepal 2025, led by Powershift Nepal with partners, engaged around 500 children and young people through virtual, provincial and national events and produced a statement that fed into Nepal's COP 30 priorities and YOUNGO's Global Youth Statement.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
380 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 194 0 R
/T (LCOY Nepal 2026 was held as a three-day residential conference at Anupam Foodland, Battisputali, Kathmandu, on 14, 15 and 16 August 2026. It was open to children and youth aged 10 to 30, with priority given to marginalised, indigenous and ethnic communities, differently-abled individuals, children, women and those directly affected by climate and social adversity. A minimum of 50 percent women and gender-diverse participation was applied to the selection process ensuring that inclusion and equitable representation remained a significant consideration throughout the conference. )
/E (LCOY Nepal 2026 was held as a three-day residential conference at Anupam Foodland, Battisputali, Kathmandu, on 14, 15 and 16 August 2026. It was open to children and youth aged 10 to 30, with priority given to marginalised, indigenous and ethnic communities, differently-abled individuals, children, women and those directly affected by climate and social adversity. A minimum of 50 percent women and gender-diverse participation was applied to the selection process ensuring that inclusion and equitable representation remained a significant consideration throughout the conference. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
381 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 194 0 R
/T (The theme, "Together for Climate Transparency", was introduced by the focal point at the opening plenary. Transparency was framed as three things at once: honesty about what is happening on the ground, correct and shared information about what is being promised and spent, and a guarantee that every voice in the room reaches the table where decisions are made.)
/E (The theme, "Together for Climate Transparency", was introduced by the focal point at the opening plenary. Transparency was framed as three things at once: honesty about what is happening on the ground, correct and shared information about what is being promised and spent, and a guarantee that every voice in the room reaches the table where decisions are made.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
