702 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 203 0 R
/E (The session examined the intersection of climate change and sexual and reproductive health and rights \(SRHR\), emphasising that climate change extends beyond environmental impacts and has differentiated consequences across gender and social groups. Using an online quiz and open discussion, participants reflected on which communities are most affected by climate change and how SRHR should be integrated into climate discourse. Discussions highlighted the disproportionate  )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
703 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 203 0 R
/T (Sanju Lamichhane - Department of Water Supply and Sewerage Management: Sanju Lamichhane highlighted the importance of grounding climate planning in localized analysis to understand specific climate impacts, while noting that limited resources remain a key gap. She emphasized the need for design analysis and emergency response planning across all offices, along with multi-stakeholder communication on WASH, sanitation, and water issues. She also stressed the importance of involving children in these processes from the very beginning.)
/E (Sanju Lamichhane - Department of Water Supply and Sewerage Management: Sanju Lamichhane highlighted the importance of grounding climate planning in localized analysis to understand specific climate impacts, while noting that limited resources remain a key gap. She emphasized the need for design analysis and emergency response planning across all offices, along with multi-stakeholder communication on WASH, sanitation, and water issues. She also stressed the importance of involving children in these processes from the very beginning.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
