720 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (Delegates and children then worked in groups across five thematic stations focusing on disaster- and climate-resilient infrastructure, curriculum and knowledge, education continuity during emergencies, teacher and student capacity, and climate financing and accountability. Discussions called for stronger regulation of school site selection and construction, inclusive infrastructure for children and persons with disabilities, geography-specific infrastructure standards, and effective enforcement of disaster-resilient building guidelines. Participants also emphasised integrating traditional and local knowledge into curricula, strengthening practical disaster-response education, improving teacher and student preparedness, and ensuring accessible early-warning systems and continuity mechanisms during emergencies. On financing, participants highlighted the need for greater domestic investment, transparency, public auditing, and community ownership of climate-related education funds.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
