/E (Participants discussed economic and non-economic losses, including impacts on agriculture, infrastructure, employment, biodiversity, health, cultural identity, traditional knowledge, social cohesion, and human life. The session then explored just energy transition, focusing on benefit sharing, import substitution, GESI, grid connectivity, and FPIC. Barriers such as unfulfilled employment promises and consultation without meaningful consent were highlighted. Concerns around electric vehicle battery waste further emphasised the need for a transition grounded not only in emissions reduction, but also in environmental and social justice.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
