772 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (The discussion identified key gaps, including the absence of meaningful youth participation during policy formulation, dedicated youth representation or focal points within climate governance structures, provisions addressing climate-induced youth migration, mandatory climate education, pathways to green employment, accessible youth climate finance, and youth and child specific monitoring indicators. These gaps were used to develop recommendations through a youth policy lab and survey, positioning young people as active reviewers rather than passive consultees. Key recommendations included institutionalizing youth participation in decision-making, establishing a youth focal person within the Climate Change Management Division, supporting youth-led local resilience initiatives, expanding green jobs and innovation, creating accessible youth climate finance mechanisms, investing in climate education, strengthening environmental review processes, and integrating Indigenous and local knowledge.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
