<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 208 0 R
/E (The discussion also highlighted non-economic losses that cannot be adequately captured through monetary valuation. Using the example of chauri herders in Upper Mustang, the speaker described how declining snowfall and shrinking grasslands have contributed to reduced chauri herding and youth outmigration, threatening the transmission of traditional songs, practices, and cultural knowledge between generations. This illustrated that climate loss extends beyond infrastructure and financial damage to include culture, identity, knowledge, and human lives.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
