<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 209 0 R
/E (Sulochana Khanal - Gender, Disaster and Rescue: Sulochana Khanal discussed how climate and disaster impacts differ according to gender, resources, and geography, with women and girls facing increased risks of violence during and after disasters. She challenged the perception of communities as passive victims, noting that women within affected communities are often already involved in rescue and response but remain underrepresented in formal disaster management structures. She called for greater representation of women and youth in municipal)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
842 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 209 0 R
/E (and district disaster management committees and emphasised that response strategies must reflect diverse lived experiences and needs rather than applying a uniform approach. She also highlighted the importance of integrating sexual and reproductive health and rights \(SRHR\) into climate and disaster planning.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
