/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 2666 0 R
/T (Pragya Devkota \(World Food Forum Nepal\): Pragya Devkota emphasized food security as an immediate casualty of climate shocks, noting that shifting youth perceptions of farming requires treating young people as strategic partners and financial decision-makers rather than passive beneficiaries. She highlighted climate-resilient startups as practical entry points for youth-led climate finance.)
/E (Pragya Devkota \(World Food Forum Nepal\): Pragya Devkota emphasized food security as an immediate casualty of climate shocks, noting that shifting youth perceptions of farming requires treating young people as strategic partners and financial decision-makers rather than passive beneficiaries. She highlighted climate-resilient startups as practical entry points for youth-led climate finance.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1052 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 2667 0 R
/T (Binod Deuba Thakuri \(Gen Z activist\): Binod Deuba argued that climate change is fundamentally a political issue intrinsically tied to good governance, criticizing the siloed treatment of environmental ministries and the persistent lack of budget integration. He also challenged internal inequalities within the movement, pointing out Kathmandu-centric privilege, stagnant leadership pipelines where the same faces repeatedly attend COP, and the systemic hurdles preventing true representation.)
/E (Binod Deuba Thakuri \(Gen Z activist\): Binod Deuba argued that climate change is fundamentally a political issue intrinsically tied to good governance, criticizing the siloed treatment of environmental ministries and the persistent lack of budget integration. He also challenged internal inequalities within the movement, pointing out Kathmandu-centric privilege, stagnant leadership pipelines where the same faces repeatedly attend COP, and the systemic hurdles preventing true representation.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1053 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 2668 0 R
/T (Satish Karn \(WeltHungerHilfe Nepal\): Satish Karn addressed the prevalence of tokenistic empowerment, urging young people to actively demand seats at local and national tables through eco-clubs, ward mechanisms, and funding proposals. He reframed migration around equity, stressing that structural gaps, such as unpaid internships and lack of domestic assets, force unsafe migration out of necessity.)
/E (Satish Karn \(WeltHungerHilfe Nepal\): Satish Karn addressed the prevalence of tokenistic empowerment, urging young people to actively demand seats at local and national tables through eco-clubs, ward mechanisms, and funding proposals. He reframed migration around equity, stressing that structural gaps, such as unpaid internships and lack of domestic assets, force unsafe migration out of necessity.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1054 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 2669 0 R
/T (Jyotsna Basnet \(Practical Action Nepal\): Jyotsna Basnet critiqued traditional project designs for over-indexing on physical infrastructure while neglecting community sustainability \("software"\) after project timelines expire. Advocating for a co-partner model, she underscored platforms like Local Conference of Youth \(LCOY\) as vital spaces for cross-provincial knowledge sharing and bridging grassroots realities with institutional policy.)
/E (Jyotsna Basnet \(Practical Action Nepal\): Jyotsna Basnet critiqued traditional project designs for over-indexing on physical infrastructure while neglecting community sustainability \("software"\) after project timelines expire. Advocating for a co-partner model, she underscored platforms like Local Conference of Youth \(LCOY\) as vital spaces for cross-provincial knowledge sharing and bridging grassroots realities with institutional policy.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [7]
>>
