1160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (Delegates overwhelmingly agreed that climate change can create opportunities for young entrepreneurs. A live poll identified key community-level impacts, including water insecurity and drying springs, erratic rainfall, heat stress, food insecurity, waste management challenges, declining soil health, and increasing agricultural pests. These challenges were reframed as potential opportunities for innovation and enterprise.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (The session highlighted four questions for turning problems into viable solutions: Who experiences the problem? What do they actually need? Who pays for the solution? How can we test it? Potential areas for youth-led social enterprises in Nepal included resilient tourism and culture, climate-smart agriculture, water and WASH, nature-based enterprises, and clean energy.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
