/T (12.5 Closing Plenary and Announcement of the National Children and Youth Statement)
/E (12.5 Closing Plenary and Announcement of the National Children and Youth Statement)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (The closing plenary brought together reflections from children, youth representatives, partners, and organisers on the three-day LCOY Nepal 2026 experience. A Class 8 child representative shared her appreciation for being included, noting that she initially viewed the programme as a chore but left having met new people and learned about climate change and transparency. She recommended that future programmes continue to provide meaningful spaces for children.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (Roshni Adhikari of BYAN thanked the organisers and participants for creating an inclusive platform, while stressing that inclusion should not become a tokenistic exercise and encouraging delegates to reach out to those who were not represented.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (Manashree Newa of ICIMOD encouraged delegates to recognise their collective achievement and take the learning back to their communities. She highlighted two key foundations for evidence-based advocacy: lived experience and research, pointing to Himal Talk as an accessible resource for further learning.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
