1271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 225 0 R
/T (LCOY Nepal 2026 was built on a specific bet: that the most useful thing a youth climate conference can do is not raise awareness but raise the standard of evidence young people bring to the table. The theme, "Together for Climate Transparency", was carried into practice through sessions that gave delegates numbers they could cite, methods they could use and cases they could name.)
/E (LCOY Nepal 2026 was built on a specific bet: that the most useful thing a youth climate conference can do is not raise awareness but raise the standard of evidence young people bring to the table. The theme, "Together for Climate Transparency", was carried into practice through sessions that gave delegates numbers they could cite, methods they could use and cases they could name.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
1272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 225 0 R
/T (By the end of the three days, delegates could describe Nepal's warming rate and its variation by region, the mechanics of glacial lake formation and the losses from the Thame event, why 20 percent of Kavre's springs have dried and where a recharge pond should and should not be built, the distinction between economic and non-economic loss and why cultural heritage sits in the second category, what the ICJ advisory opinion changes about state obligation, and how consensus decision-making at COP differs from majority voting. They could also test their own water and report the result.)
/E (By the end of the three days, delegates could describe Nepal's warming rate and its variation by region, the mechanics of glacial lake formation and the losses from the Thame event, why 20 percent of Kavre's springs have dried and where a recharge pond should and should not be built, the distinction between economic and non-economic loss and why cultural heritage sits in the second category, what the ICJ advisory opinion changes about state obligation, and how consensus decision-making at COP differs from majority voting. They could also test their own water and report the result.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
1273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 225 0 R
/T (The conference was equally clear about its own limits. A delegate asked why there was no child on the panel discussing children, and the organisers accepted the criticism rather than deflecting it. A delegate named the people missing from every inclusion list, including those living on the street. Panelists named the privilege inside the youth climate movement itself: that the same faces travel to COP, that leadership is not transferred, and that media attention concentrates on Kathmandu while activity happens across the country. These were not comfortable observations, and they belong in the record precisely because they are the work that remains.)
/E (The conference was equally clear about its own limits. A delegate asked why there was no child on the panel discussing children, and the organisers accepted the criticism rather than deflecting it. A delegate named the people missing from every inclusion list, including those living on the street. Panelists named the privilege inside the youth climate movement itself: that the same faces travel to COP, that leadership is not transferred, and that media attention concentrates on Kathmandu while activity happens across the country. These were not comfortable observations, and they belong in the record precisely because they are the work that remains.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
1274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 225 0 R
/T (The National Children and Youth Statement on Climate Change 2026 now moves to the Government of Nepal, into the review of the National Climate Change Policy 2019, and to YOUNGO for the Global Youth Statement ahead of COP 31 in Antalya. The Minister's invitation to bring findings to the ministry for discussion is an opening, and openings close. As the focal point told delegates in the closing plenary, the success of this conference is determined at ground level, not in the hall.)
/E (The National Children and Youth Statement on Climate Change 2026 now moves to the Government of Nepal, into the review of the National Climate Change Policy 2019, and to YOUNGO for the Global Youth Statement ahead of COP 31 in Antalya. The Minister's invitation to bring findings to the ministry for discussion is an opening, and openings close. As the focal point told delegates in the closing plenary, the success of this conference is determined at ground level, not in the hall.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [16]
>>
