5572 0 obj
<<
/Title (Nepal contributes a negligible share of global greenhouse gas emissions and carries a disproportionate share of the consequences. National temperature is rising by roughly 0.056 degrees Celsius per year, with the rate crossing the 0.1 threshold in the mountain region. Fifty of Nepal's seventy-seven districts are classified as high to very high vulnerability. Between 1996 and 2019, an average of 619 people died each year from climate-related impacts, and roughly 70 percent of those impacts were flood-induced. On a single day in August 2026, the temperature in Nepalgunj stood at 45 degrees Celsius while Namche recorded 12.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5555 0 R
/Next 5589 0 R
>>
endobj
