/Title (LCOY Nepal 2026 brought delegates from all seven provinces to Kathmandu from 14 to 16 August 2026 under the theme "Together for Climate Transparency". The conference was organized by Nepalese Youth for Climate Action \(NYCA\) and Youth Action for Sustainable and Eco Nepal \(YASEN\), with endorsement from YOUNGO. It followed nine virtual consultations that gathered climate concerns and recommendations from around 180 delegates before the residential event began.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5555 0 R
/Prev 5572 0 R
/Next 5610 0 R
>>
endobj
5590 0 obj
<<
/Title (Two demands surfaced in almost every session. First, that children and youth participation stop being tokenistic: delegates repeatedly distinguish between being counted and being consulted, and asked to be present in planning and problem-solving rather than invited as observers and advisors. Second, that transparency be treated as infrastructure rather than a slogan, with accessible data on climate finance flows, project results and local budget allocation. As one panelist put it during the transparency session, youth are not an audience, they are an accountability force.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5555 0 R
/Prev 5611 0 R
/Next 5573 0 R
>>
endobj
