5612 0 obj
<<
/Title (Nepal has hosted an LCOY every year since 2022. LCOY Nepal 2022 was held virtually and engaged more than 60 young people directly and over 2,000 indirectly. LCOY Nepal 2023, themed "Vision to Action", brought together participants from all seven provinces with more than half of them women. LCOY Nepal 2024, organised by YASEN and Sustainability Week Kathmandu under the theme "From Local to Global", convened 190 participants and focused on NDCs, loss and damage and indigenous knowledge. LCOY Nepal 2025, led by Powershift Nepal with partners, engaged around 500 children and young people through virtual, provincial and national events and produced a statement that fed into Nepal's COP 30 priorities and YOUNGO's Global Youth Statement.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5574 0 R
/Prev 5592 0 R
/Next 5636 0 R
>>
endobj
5613 0 obj
<<
/Title (The theme, "Together for Climate Transparency", was introduced by the focal point at the opening plenary. Transparency was framed as three things at once: honesty about what is happening on the ground, correct and shared information about what is being promised and spent, and a guarantee that every voice in the room reaches the table where decisions are made.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5574 0 R
/Prev 5636 0 R
/Next 5593 0 R
>>
