/Title (By the end of the three days, delegates could describe Nepal's warming rate and its variation by region, the mechanics of glacial lake formation and the losses from the Thame event, why 20 percent of Kavre's springs have dried and where a recharge pond should and should not be built, the distinction between economic and non-economic loss and why cultural heritage sits in the second category, what the ICJ advisory opinion changes about state obligation, and how consensus decision-making at COP differs from majority voting. They could also test their own water and report the result.)
/Dest [45 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5575 0 R
/Prev 5596 0 R
/Next 5648 0 R
>>
endobj
