<<
/Title (Jyotsna Basnet \(Practical Action Nepal\): Jyotsna Basnet critiqued traditional project designs for over-indexing on physical infrastructure while neglecting community sustainability \("software"\) after project timelines expire. Advocating for a co-partner model, she underscored platforms like Local Conference of Youth \(LCOY\) as vital spaces for cross-provincial knowledge sharing and bridging grassroots realities with institutional policy.)
/Dest [37 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5619 0 R
/Prev 5708 0 R
/Next 5734 0 R
>>
endobj
5734 0 obj
<<
/Title (During the rapid-fire segment, panelists defined climate justice through inclusive decision-making, favored the energy of the street over the table, and identified tokenism as the single greatest obstacle facing youth advocacy.)
/Dest [37 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5619 0 R
/Prev 5733 0 R
/Next 5709 0 R
>>
endobj
5735 0 obj
<<
/Title (The process emphasised collective ownership of the statement, ensuring that it was not simply prepared on behalf of children and youth, but shaped through their direct participation and contributions. Through discussion, feedback, and refinement, participants worked towards a final statement that consolidated their shared concerns, priorities, and demands for climate action in Nepal.)
/Dest [42 0 R /Fit]
